From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:40:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] A building's sun shadow follows the ground's heights; no sun
 shadows under a roof (SDK_PORT_3DS)

A building's shadow was one flat outline at the height it stands at, and
a copy for up to two higher heights, each drawn wherever nothing stood in
front of it: over lower ground it hung in the air and showed somewhere
else (the Galactic building's down the stepped wall beside its plaza, a
dish's in pieces), and lower ground had no shadow of its own.

Now the ground under and beside the outline is looked up as a grid of the
map's tiles (the field's own heights; a tile not known yet is the
building's own ground, and the grid is looked at again every 90 frames
until all are known). Up to 6 heights, the building's own and those found
most often within 64 of it, above or below; for each the shadow of what
stands above that height (NitroPort_Gx3dShadowHullPartsFrom), cut to the
tiles at that height (NitroPort_Gx3dShadowPieces): each piece lies on its
own ground. Kept as two display lists (the shade, its soft edge) for the
building's place until the sun moves on, one building's made a frame.
On ground all at the building's own height the outline is drawn whole, as
before.

Under a roof (the area's lighting not the outdoors') the port is told
there is no sun (NitroPort_SetSunRoofed): nothing is marked, everything is
drawn as the DS has it. A lobby's planters cast the sun's wedges across
its floor.
